+# Secure-Aggregation Crypto Review Plan (scaffold)
+
+Objective: validate the cryptographic protocol and implementation for secure aggregation before enabling production FL rounds.
+
+Steps:
+1) Implementation selection
+   - Choose audited implementation (google/secagg or vetted commercial lib).
+   - Obtain library source and audit artifacts.
+2) Build & test in isolated builder
+   - Use ops/fl/integration/secagg_install.sh in an isolated build host to produce wheel/artifact.
+   - Install into FL images and run ops/fl/tests/secagg_integration_test.py.
+3) Scale tests
+   - Run ops/fl/tests/scale_secagg_simulation.py with 100+ clients (CI lane).
+   - Run dropout scenarios: randomly kill X% clients mid-round and verify reconstruction.
+4) Adversary tests
+   - Simulate malicious clients sending malformed updates; verify robust aggregator rejects or tolerates.
+5) Review & audit
+   - Engage external cryptographer to review design, implementation, and key management.
+   - Collect review artifacts and upload to S3/Rekor.
+6) Sign-off & enable
+   - Only enable secure-aggregation in production after auditor sign-off and CI passes.
+
